==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|strecken}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|strecken}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*strakjaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*(s)treg-||rigid, stiff}}. Compare Dutch {{m|nl|strekken}}, Low German {{m|nds|streken}}, English {{m|en|stretch}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈʃtʁɛkŋ̩]|[ˈʃtʁɛkən]|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-weak|streckt|streckte|gestreckt}}

# to [[straighten]], [[stretch]]
#: ''Sie streckte ihre müden Glieder.'' - She stretched her tired limbs.
# to [[elongate]], [[lengthen]]
# to [[dilute]], [[cut]]
#: ''Er streckte den Wein mit Wasser.'' - He diluted the wine with water.

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj-weak|streck|gestreckt|h}}

